  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 316 AM MDT Sat Jun 20 2026\n\nAn upper level trof is moving through Idaho today and will bring\nisolated to scattered showers and thunderstorms. There is a 50\npercent chance some of the central mountains could see over 0.10\ninches of rain and some eastern mountain areas by Sunday\nmorning. But overall is starting out very dry so little risk at\nall of significant precipitation unless a very strong\nthunderstorm develops. It will be much cooler today with highs\nmainly 60s and 70s mountains and 70s to lower 80s valleys. Will\nbe breezy in the Eastern Magic Valley and Snake River Plain with\n25 to 35 mph wind gusts expected. Sunday will see only isolated\nshowers and thunderstorms in the eastern mountains with minimal\nchances elsewhere. Monday through Friday will be dry with a\nwarming trend with high temperatures 5 to 10 degrees above\nnormal Tuesday into Thursday. After Sunday no precipitation\nexpected until next weekend at the earliest.",
